# VERCEL DEPLOY RULE - MUST FOLLOW - FREE TIER 100/DAY

## 1. NEVER double deploy
- DO NOT run `vercel --prod --yes` if you already did `git push origin main` for same commit
- GitHub auto-deploy = 1 deploy. CLI vercel --prod = 1 deploy. Doing both = 2x waste.
- RULE: Use ONLY `git push origin main` - NEVER use `vercel --prod --yes` unless user says "deploy via CLI only" and quota <80

## 2. Check quota BEFORE any deploy
Before any git push or vercel deploy, run:
```
vercel ls --limit 100 | grep -c "2026-08-27\|Today"
```
If count >80: STOP, warn user "80/100 used, batch remaining fixes into 1 commit, wait until 06:00 AM BST reset"
If count >95: DO NOT DEPLOY AT ALL, only local `npm run build`

## 3. Batch fixes into 1 commit
- DO NOT create 3 commits 8ab2552, 64d3962, 20fa804 for same task
- Combine security + Bangla + functional into ONE commit: `git add . && git commit -m "fix: ..."`
- Use `git commit --amend` if last commit not pushed yet
- NEVER `git push --force` with rebase - it cancels + recreates deploys = counts double

## 4. Local verify, not prod verify
- Always `npm run build` locally -> 87.7kB green before push
- Curl verify on local `http://localhost:3000` not on hostamar.com prod
- Prod curl only AFTER Ready, not as deploy trigger

## 5. Daily limit reset
- Reset is 00:00 UTC = 06:00 AM BST Bangladesh
- If hit `api-deployments-free-per-day`, tell user wait until tomorrow 06:00 AM BST, do NOT retry vercel --prod loop

## 6. Guard script
Run `bash scripts/check-vercel-quota.sh` before push - script returns exit 1 if >90
